# Vendored tree — bytes exactly as they came from upstream.
#
# This machine's gitconfig sets core.autocrlf=input, which normalises CRLF to
# LF on the way into the index. For our own code that is what we want; here it
# is not. 105 of the end-4 SVGs ship with CRLF, and normalising them makes the
# tree stop being byte-identical to the commit recorded in UPSTREAM. The
# refetch described there works by diffing against a clean copy — with
# normalisation that diff shows 105 files nobody touched, and the signal that
# matters (what WE changed, ADR-0009) is buried in the noise.
#
# -text disables end-of-line conversion for this subtree.
* -text
